  "articleBody": "Knowing when to tackle a log home interior staining project yourself versus calling in a pro can save you a lot of grief (and money!). While a small, straightforward section might be a DIY weekend project, there are definite signs it’s time to bring in the experts. For example, if you've got widespread peeling or large, faded areas all over your logs, that's a big indicator. It means there's likely a lot of prep work, like sanding or stripping, that needs to happen for a uniform finish. Another red flag is if your logs have mixed prior coatings. Trying to stain over different types of old finishes can lead to an uneven look or compatibility issues, and a professional knows how to handle that. If you're unsure about the best way to remove old stains, or how to ensure a truly uniform finish across all your interior log surfaces, a qualified log-home finisher can make all the difference. Sometimes, the peace of mind and guaranteed quality from an experienced team like HH Remodeling is worth every penny.",
  "datePublished": "2026-08-09"
}